          "type": "event",
          "value": "Graduation",
          "context": "Bernard Andreae graduated from Marburg in 1956 under Friedrich Matz, specializing in Roman sarcophagi; his thesis analyzed historical motifs within sarcophagus iconography."
        },
        {
          "type": "role",
          "value": "Assistant",
          "context": "From 1956 to 1959, he served as Assistant at the German Archaeological Institute in Italy.",
          "from": "1956",
